# SymbiYosys job for eog_features (spec/modules/eog_features.md, numerics.md §4, spec v4). Verify role, task
# T1.features.fv.     bash scripts/formal.sh features
# Harness fv_eog_features.sv (property list F1-F6 + stage contract in its header). N_FAC = 2, N_WELL = 8.
#
# prove     k-induction with the abstract multiplier (formal/common/eog_mul_abstract.sv): stage contract
#           (u_stage.st_*, incl. II <= 16 and latency <= 128), handshake (u_out.ax_*), F1, F2, F3, F4_zero, F5, F6,
#           B_*. Unbounded.
# prove_f4  k-induction with the stand-in multiplier formal/features/eog_mul_concat.sv: F4_ch / F4_sat bit-exact
#           against the rounding / saturation reference, plus everything `prove` checks. Unbounded. (Why a stand-in:
#           see eog_mul_concat.sv; eog_mul = a*b itself is proven by formal/mul.)
# cover     the real rtl/eog_mul.sv: a saturated channel (C_sat), SHUT_IN (C_shutin), channel 11 nonzero (C_ch11), a
#           second record (C_two), held back-pressure (C_bp).
# No bmc task: F4 against the real multiplier would need SAT to prove the DUT's 20x32 eog_mul equal to a reference
# x*M, which did not finish (bitwuzla stalled > 4 min at the first output step even with every reading and P0
# limited to [-2, 2]; T1.mul.fv saw the same at 16x16). The spec's alternative is used instead: prove_f4 checks the
# rounding / saturation step bit-exactly around a stand-in product, formal/mul proves eog_mul = a*b, and
# tb/features checks the real composition bit for bit on every golden record (incl. the saturation corner cases).
#
# Depths: k-induction needs depth > the design's own accept-to-output latency and accept-to-accept interval (not
# II_MAX / LAT_MAX: the checker's wait counters are reset by the design's progress within that window). A design
# that takes longer per record needs a larger prove depth (or internal invariants under ifdef FORMAL).
# prove / prove_f4 depth 20: against a throwaway one-record-at-a-time stub (accept-to-output 13 cycles, accept wait 13)
# induction closed at length ~14; 20 leaves room for a design up to ~18 cycles per record. cover depth 40: C_two
# (second record out) needs ~2 x latency + 3 steps (step 29 on the stub); the other goals step 15.
# Measured on the stub (WSL, bitwuzla, machine shared with other jobs): spec v4 prove 83 s, prove_f4 296 s,
# cover 30 s (v1: 247 s, 493 s, 31 s).
# The harness was checked against stub mutants (each caught by bmc at depth 17): SHUT_IN ignoring water -> F5_si;
# v1-style rules on INVALID records -> F1_zero, F5_pf; channel 11 without PREV_OK -> F3_ch11; rounding dropped ->
# F4_ch; FEAT_SAT ignoring channels 9-11 -> F4_sat (the last two on the v1 stub).
# Engine: bitwuzla. yices stalled for > 5 min on the first output step of a 16-step bmc that bitwuzla and boolector
# finish in ~15 s (the 373-bit records and 512-bit CONFIG rows suit word-level solvers).

[tasks]
prove
prove_f4
cover

[options]
prove:    mode prove
prove:    depth 20
prove_f4: mode prove
prove_f4: depth 20
cover:    mode cover
cover:    depth 40

[engines]
smtbmc bitwuzla

[script]
prove:    read_verilog -formal -sv -DFV_ABSTRACT_MUL eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul_abstract.sv eog_features.sv fv_eog_features.sv
prove_f4: read_verilog -formal -sv -DFV_CONCAT_MUL eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul_concat.sv eog_features.sv fv_eog_features.sv
cover:    read_verilog -formal -sv -DFV_COVER eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul.sv eog_features.sv fv_eog_features.sv
prep -top fv_eog_features

[files]
../../rtl/eog_defs.svh
../../rtl/eog_features.sv
../../rtl/eog_mul.sv
../common/eog_fv_props.sv
../common/eog_mul_abstract.sv
eog_mul_concat.sv
fv_eog_features.sv
